Custom Results Reports - Acceptance Criteria
User Story (i)
 As a centre user
 I want to filter which candidates' results are included in my report
 So that I only generate a file for the series, centre, qualification and syllabus I need

Acceptance Criteria
Filter controls are available
AC1. 
GIVEN I am on the Download Results screen
WHEN the page loads
THEN I see filter controls for Series, Centre, Qualification and Syllabus, each defaulting to a sensible value
Filters update the report live
AC2. 
GIVEN I have the Download Results screen open
WHEN I change any filter
THEN the preview and the file that will be downloaded update immediately without a page reload
Qualification and Syllabus support All
AC3. 
GIVEN I am setting filters
WHEN I open the Qualification or Syllabus filter
THEN I can choose All to include every qualification or syllabus the centre is entered for
Reports are scoped to one centre
AC4. 
GIVEN I am signed in
WHEN I use the Download Results screen
THEN I can only generate files for centres I have been granted access to
No matching candidates warning
AC5. 
GIVEN I have set filters
WHEN the filter combination matches zero candidates
THEN I am told clearly before I can configure fields or attempt a download
User Story (ii)
 As a centre user
 I want to choose which extra details are included in my file, in addition to the fields every file must contain
 So that the file matches what my downstream system or colleagues need

Acceptance Criteria
Standard fields always included
AC1. 
GIVEN I open the Download Results screen
WHEN I view the Standard fields panel
THEN I see Centre number, Series, Candidate number, Candidate name and UCI listed, and I cannot switch any of them off
Standard fields are marked as locked
AC2. 
GIVEN I view the Standard fields panel
WHEN the panel is displayed
THEN each standard field is shown as locked and a count of how many are always included is visible
Additional fields are grouped
AC3. 
GIVEN I view the Additional fields panel
WHEN the panel is displayed
THEN the fields are grouped into four labelled categories: Centre & qualification, Candidate details, Syllabus result, Component result
Toggle a field on or off
AC4. 
GIVEN I view an additional field in a group
WHEN I switch its toggle
THEN its label and description are shown next to the toggle, and the preview updates to include or exclude that field
Expand and collapse a group
AC5. 
GIVEN I view a field group
WHEN I click the group header
THEN the group expands or collapses, and a running count of selected fields in that group is shown
Select all or clear all
AC6. 
GIVEN I view the Additional fields panel
WHEN I click Select all or Clear all
THEN every additional field is selected or deselected accordingly, and the x of y selected total updates immediately
Selection updates the preview immediately
AC7. 
GIVEN I change a field selection
WHEN the change is made
THEN the live preview and the selected-field count update without a page reload
User Story (iii)
 As a centre user
 I want to control the order fields appear in my file
 So that the output lines up with the layout my downstream system expects

Acceptance Criteria
Standard fields stay first and fixed
AC1. 
GIVEN I view the Standard fields panel
WHEN I look at the field order
THEN the five standard fields always appear first, in a fixed order that cannot be changed
Reorder fields within a group
AC2. 
GIVEN I have fields in a group
WHEN I drag a field, or use its move up / move down controls
THEN the field moves to its new position within the group and the preview updates immediately
Reorder whole groups
AC3. 
GIVEN I view the Additional fields panel
WHEN I drag a group, or use the move up / move down controls on its header
THEN the group moves to its new position, changing which group's fields appear first among the additional columns
Reordering works without a mouse
AC4. 
GIVEN I am using a keyboard
WHEN I use the move up / move down controls on a field or group
THEN I can reorder fields and groups without needing to drag anything
Preview matches the download exactly
AC5. 
GIVEN I have set a field and group order
WHEN I compare the live preview to the downloaded file
THEN the column order is identical for every supported format
Order is sent to the export process
AC6. 
GIVEN I have set a field and group order
WHEN I download the file
THEN the chosen order is submitted as an ordered list so the generated file reproduces that exact order
Saved templates restore the order
AC7. 
GIVEN I saved a template with a specific field and group order
WHEN I re-apply that template
THEN the field selection and the exact group/field order are both restored as they were when saved
User Story (iv)
 As a centre user
 I want to choose the file format
 So that I can open the file the way I need to - spreadsheet, system import, fixed-width upload, or XML feed

Acceptance Criteria
Four formats are offered
AC1. 
GIVEN I view the Format panel
WHEN the panel is displayed
THEN I see CSV, DAT, XLSX and XML, each with a short description of what it is best for
CSV is the default
AC2. 
GIVEN I open the Download Results screen
WHEN the page loads
THEN CSV is selected by default
Format choice does not reset fields
AC3. 
GIVEN I have selected fields and an order
WHEN I switch to a different format
THEN my field selection and field order remain unchanged
CSV opens correctly in Excel
AC4. 
GIVEN I download a CSV file
WHEN I open it in Excel
THEN it opens correctly because the file includes a UTF-8 byte-order mark
DAT is fixed-width
AC5. 
GIVEN I select DAT and view the preview
WHEN the preview is shown
THEN there is no header row, every column has a defined width, and a character ruler with the total record length is displayed
XLSX is a genuine workbook
AC6. 
GIVEN I download an XLSX file
WHEN I open it
THEN it is a real workbook with one worksheet and a header row, not a renamed CSV
XML is valid and structured
AC7. 
GIVEN I download an XML file
WHEN I inspect it
THEN each result row is wrapped in a RESULT element with one child element per column, named after the column header, and the file is valid, well-formed XML
User Story (v)
 As a centre user
 I want to see a sample of my file before I download it
 So that I can check the fields, format and data look right first

Acceptance Criteria
Preview matches the file
AC1. 
GIVEN I have set fields, order and format
WHEN I view the preview
THEN it uses the exact same columns, order and formatting rules as the file that will be downloaded
Preview updates live
AC2. 
GIVEN I am viewing the preview
WHEN I change fields, field order or format
THEN the preview updates immediately
Preview rendering matches the format
AC3. 
GIVEN I have chosen a format
WHEN I view the preview
THEN CSV, DAT and XML show literal file text, and XLSX renders as a table with additional columns visually distinguished from standard ones
No results notice
AC4. 
GIVEN my filters match no candidates
WHEN I view the preview
THEN a clear no-results notice is shown and the download action is disabled
Row count is shown
AC5. 
GIVEN I have results matching my filters
WHEN I view the preview
THEN I can see the total number of matching rows, for example Showing first 4 of 4,820 rows
User Story (vi)
 As a centre user
 I want to download the finished file in one action
 So that I can save it where I need it

Acceptance Criteria
Single download action
AC1. 
GIVEN I have set fields, order and format
WHEN I click Download
THEN the file is generated and downloaded using my current selection
Downloading state prevents duplicates
AC2. 
GIVEN I click Download
WHEN the file is being produced
THEN the button shows a Downloading state and is disabled so I cannot trigger a duplicate request
File name identifies centre and series
AC3. 
GIVEN I download a file
WHEN I check its file name
THEN it identifies the centre and series, for example results_A23DT9_June2026.csv
Clear error on failure
AC4. 
GIVEN my download request fails
WHEN I see the result
THEN I am shown a clear error notice, I can retry, and no partial or corrupt file is saved to my device
Large files build in the background
AC5. 
GIVEN I request a large file
WHEN I click Download
THEN the file is generated in the background and I can keep working while it is prepared
My reports shows status
AC6. 
GIVEN I have requested one or more files
WHEN I open My reports
THEN each file is listed with a clear status - Queued, Generating or Ready - and I can download it once it is Ready
Files expire after a retention period
AC7. 
GIVEN a background-generated file has been ready for a defined period
WHEN the retention period passes
THEN the file is no longer available to download
User Story (vii)
 As a centre user
 I want to save my format and field selection as a named template
 So that I can reuse it next time instead of starting from a blank page

Acceptance Criteria
Save the current selection
AC1. 
GIVEN I have set a format and field selection
WHEN I choose to save it as a template and give it a name
THEN the template is saved and listed under Saved templates
Re-apply a template
AC2. 
GIVEN I have one or more saved templates
WHEN I select a saved template
THEN its format and field selection are applied immediately
Delete a template
AC3. 
GIVEN I have a saved template
WHEN I delete it
THEN it is removed from the list, and the Saved templates section disappears once none remain
Templates are private to the centre
AC4. 
GIVEN I am signed in to a centre
WHEN I view Saved templates
THEN I only see templates saved for that centre
Template limit is enforced
AC5. 
GIVEN my centre already has 10 (configurable) saved templates
WHEN I save a new template
THEN the oldest template is discarded to keep the total at 10
Template captures order
AC6. 
GIVEN I save a template with a specific field and group order
WHEN I re-apply that template later
THEN the exact column order is restored, not only which fields were selected
User Story (viii)
 As a centre user
 I want to share a template with named colleagues or a team
 So that we use the same report definition without sharing underlying data

Acceptance Criteria
Share with named colleagues or a team
AC1. 
GIVEN I have a saved template
WHEN I choose to share it
THEN I can share it with one or more named colleagues, or with a team
Only the selection is shared
AC2. 
GIVEN I have shared a template
WHEN a colleague uses it
THEN they see only their own centre's data; the underlying results data is never shared
Permission levels
AC3. 
GIVEN I am sharing a template
WHEN I set a permission for a colleague or team
THEN I can choose Can use (apply only) or Can edit (can change it for everyone it is shared with)
Edits propagate to everyone
AC4. 
GIVEN a shared template has Can edit permission
WHEN the owner edits it
THEN everyone it is shared with sees the updated version
Duplicate to keep a private copy
AC5. 
GIVEN a template has been shared with me
WHEN I duplicate it
THEN I get my own private copy that other people's edits will not affect
User Story (ix)
 As a centre user
 I want to sign in once and only see data for centres I am permitted to access
 So that my reports stay secure and relevant

Acceptance Criteria
Sign in with SAP CDC
AC1. 
GIVEN I open the portal
WHEN I am not signed in
THEN I sign in through the organisation's SAP CDC identity provider, with multi-factor authentication where enabled, and no separate portal password is needed
Centres are loaded and enforced
AC2. 
GIVEN I have signed in
WHEN the portal loads
THEN only the centres I am permitted to access are available for filtering, preview and download
Sessions refresh while active
AC3. 
GIVEN I am signed in and working
WHEN my session nears expiry
THEN it refreshes automatically; signing out ends the session
No-access message
AC4. 
GIVEN I do not have access to Download Results
WHEN I try to open the screen
THEN I see a clear no-access message instead of the report screen
User Story (x)
 As a product owner
 I want the feature to be reliable, accessible and well tested
 So that it can be released with confidence

Acceptance Criteria
Full keyboard operability
AC1. 
GIVEN I am using a keyboard only
WHEN I interact with toggles, buttons and drag handles
THEN every control is reachable and operable, with a visible focus state
Assistive technology announcements
AC2. 
GIVEN I am using assistive technology
WHEN a field, group or format selection changes
THEN the updated counts and selections are announced
Performance at full scale
AC3. 
GIVEN a centre has its full results set loaded, not sample data
WHEN I filter, preview or download
THEN the page remains responsive
Automated test coverage
AC4. 
GIVEN the feature is built
WHEN the test suite runs
THEN it covers field selection and toggling, field and group reordering, format switching, preview rendering per format, template save/apply/delete, and the download success and error paths
Layouts validated with downstream systems
AC5. 
GIVEN the DAT fixed-width layout is finalised
WHEN it is checked against downstream systems' expected layouts
THEN it is validated before general release
